 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "trades are records [timestamp, symbol, direction, quantity, price] of strings, in time order; direction is \"B\" or \"S\"; quantity and price are positive integers. Cash starts at 1000. A buy subtracts quantity * price from cash and adds the shares; a sell adds q * price to cash and removes q shares, where q is the quantity clamped to the shares currently held (inferred). Every trade sets the latest price of its symbol. Return [[\"CASH\", cash], [symbol, shares], ...] with numbers as decimal strings, holdings with zero shares removed, symbols in ascending order. Level 1: cash may become negative.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
